        <p>Another of those wonderful cures of skin-die,,c that have set the seal on Zam-Buk's fame as a herbal healer of unprecedented power has just ,ch°l:ro- to light in London. Eczema had run throughfe of generations of the family of Mrs. E. Cronin, 01,'„et. a colour printer, of 21. Victoria-road, Higll-9'' of- Plaistow, E., and despite the best .endeayourste doctors and hospital specialists the disease %or' neither be cured -nor its growth checked until JatO Buk comp W completely Stamped out the hereditary ell' Mrs. Cronin, her daughters, and _grandchildre; n. „tetl' .To a London journalist who specially inve't`er". this remarkable case, Mrs. Cronin, who is said i--" When I was 25 I began to suffer from eciess which I believe I got from a second-hand dtreittla bought. After the first time I wore the dress 1 -I°)cify . my forearms itched very much, and soon- thr,t.heO, became inflamed. I bee me positively alarrne" , these burning p.tches spread to my legs. ho and face. Some of the inflamed places wore o--theil as a saucer The Rh:it burned and smarted, and died away and peeled off. " A doctor told me I had contracted a verf form of skin disease, which it would probal":', impossible to cure. For two years I atteade%o surgery twice a week, and used the ointment lie beat. rie, but there was not the slightest inlPr°veLl'e Then I went for a long time to St. Bartholo93;t‘P Hospital, and afterwards I attended other .11°,51);t and dispensaries and several private doctors. 14' the end of 25 years' careful treatment my skal still eovered with the burning and itching disco lidrell " What was worse, three out of four of inY C' u 1,1 frbO' born after I had contracted the eczema suffero of.. the same disease, and two grandchildren, ollifare scri). ethree' different daughters, also suffered in the san' immediately after birth. • Fortunately, about reat years ago I began to use Zam-Buk. To surprise, the rough, inflamed patches were ZeV24 Zam-Buk. Patch after patch of the ee cleared away, and always in each place a nevi grew. ess "My daughters seeing Zam-Buk's great their my case used the balm for themselves all' ze00 children. All six who were affected with the. kec sod. have now been completely cured by ZanrDufoilY' there is now rrist, a trace of the disedse Or ..aieecni9 Zam-Bult has thoroughly eured a' horrid sh;?1 atior that caused great distress amongst three gene?. of our family."</p>
