      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-25_WidnesExaminer_art0034" n="art0034">
        <head>CROWD AT THE WARRINGTON v. ST. HELENS MATCH.</head>
        <p>THE CROWD AT THE WARRINGTON v. ST. HELENS MATCH.</p>
        <p>The originals of the porraits marked with a X will receive the " Examiner " prize of ss. on calling at the (ace iii Bewsfy-street on or before Saturday next, October 2nd. Two prizes of ss. are offered for every First Team match, and one prize of ss. for every "A " Team match at Wilderspool. Last week's winner at the Warrington "A " v. P.ochdale " A " match was M. Gilligan, 19 ~,,a%oliester-road.</p>
        <p>goal-kicking in the Warrington team has been altogether too indiscriminate. It is a point Ncorthy of •serious attention, for a reliable goal-kicker is an asset of incalculable value,</p>
        <p>The "A " team again acquitted themselves well away from home, and the 20 points to 3 points victory at St. Helens is worth a clap. Cartwright was well in the scoring, and a promising display IVI given by the new full back W. B. Gibbs.</p>
        <p>I am keeping some of the best news to the last. Warrington has at last receii-ed a cablegram from an Australian wing threequarter whom O'Malley and Frawley consider in a class by himself. This player is named Stuntz, and he has responded to Warring- ton's offer by announcing his departure for Old England: Stuntz is only a young player, but an international in his own country, and credited with being able to give filly Messenger a clear 10 yards in 100. So he should be something in the nature of a flyer. In another five weeks we may see him here.</p>
        <p>Another item of interest is the signing on of Smith, the crack Stockton Heath wing threequarter, whom competent critics praise very highly. Smith is a teacher at the Beamout - School, and the type of player to do the game credit. He is sel:lted to play for the "A " team against Widnes " A "to-day. Frawley is also selected, but not much serious foot- ball can be expected from him yet. His appearance should however, qualify him for the Lancashire Cup, and there are more unlii,ely things than that he u:11 be fit and well for the first round on October 111th at Wigan.</p>
        <p>The" A " team will be Gibbs, full back ; Frawley, Cartwright, Ilockenhall and Smith threequarters ; Lloyd and Daintith, half-backs; Belton, Bradshaw, Naylor, Harrison, Chesters, and P. Boardman, forwards.</p>
        <p>The South-West Lancashire .League table up-to- date is as follows Poicts.</p>
        <p>P. W. L. D. For. Agst. Pts. Warringt-in Runt orn. Leigh St. Hele.ns 2 0 1 1 ... 20 ... 24 ... 1 ‘Vican ——— -- ... ... ... Widnes - - - - ••• - ••• ."-- ••• ..-"'"</p>
      </div>
