        <p>WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT LEAGUE. Results for September 13th. Calder and Mersey 2. TbelwJl Uuited 0. *Howley 7, Walker's Brewery 0. *Earlestown St. John's 2, Waitecross 0. WIIITECROSS SOCIAL V. EARLESTOWN Sr. JOHN'S RESERVE. These teams met at Earlestown on Saturdly, and the home team registered a victory by two goals to nil after a very hard-fought game. Matches for September 256. Howley v. Wh i t cross. • Wellfleld,v. Walker's Brewery.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT ELEMENTARY S.3llOOLi LEAGUE.</p>
        <p>This stmessful league has got into full swing again and a capital programme has Amen dravtn up for the season.</p>
        <p>An interesting game resulted from the meeting of Heathside and St. Niary's. There was ngtbing to choose between the teams as far as play went, but the height of the Heathside boss enabled them to claim vict ry by the ntrrovv margin of 1--O. Bennett pliyed a capital game for the winners, while Putter and Dombavand were the best of the losers. Braruont and Silver•street met on the gronni of the former and the home team were somewhat fortunate in winning 2-1.</p>
