      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-25_WidnesExaminer_art0045" n="art0045">
        <head>BOWLING.</head>
        <p>BOWLING.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON CEMETERY v. WARRINGTON</p>
        <p>WORKS ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>An interesting match took place cn the Bowling Green, Bank Quay .on S.iturday, when the champions ot Lancashire and Che3hire-7the Warrington Ct meters, B.C.—met a picked team from the Warfington Works Bowing Association. The proceeds were to provide a testimonial to Mr. J. Willet in leen:ll4km of his valuable services to the association daring the seven years he has been chairman. Scores :--</p>
        <p>WORKS. CEMETERY. J. Holland W. Patrick .1. Barton - 2 l 2l R. Rothwell lO J. Hutchinson 2l 'l'. Hu'mphrie. W. Roughley W. Rarcidles W. Andrews 2l W. Swanton l5 J. :Jolley R. Jefferson 2/ T. Harrison lB A. Broadhurst *.:l A. Scott (clptain) W. t.-imister (capt3in) ... 21 R. Sunderland lB B. Tomlinson</p>
        <p>223 The Works (con by 32.</p>
        <p>After the match Mr. \V. WEnsTutproposed a vote of thanks to the Cemttery for corning to Bank Quay to play. This was seconded by Mr. A. G. BOARDMAN and cal red.</p>
        <p>Mr. 0. BALL, jun., proposed a vote of thanks to Mr. Webster abd Mr. Boardman for scing as reftreee. '1 his was seconded by Mr. SCOTT and heartily accorded.</p>
        <p>ODDEFELLOWS MAIN.</p>
        <p>Saturday saw (be close of theannual main promoted by the Warrington and District branch of the Independent Order uf Ow:Bellows, Manch( ster Unity, and there was a large attendance on the green aejoiniug the King and Queen Hotel, Padgate-lane. Scores : Fl. Hey l3 W. Paskin 9 J. Shelton H. Savory w.o. H. Wright — A. Lawton D. Bromley W. Daniels W. Newton l3 T. .1. Fora Et. Allen - 13 H. ILsrum ... 8 W. Butterworth ..... .... w.o. J. T. Ellison T. Reddish .1. Dawson .. l3 A. Stretford ll H. Broadhurst ..... 13 W. Holb:ook A. Glover l3 E. Bailey 2 J. Hitchmough ... l3 J. Daintith</p>
