      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-25_WidnesExaminer_art0102" n="art0102">
        <head>ROYAL SISTERS AT COPENHAGEN.</head>
        <p>THE ROYAL SISTERS AT COPENHAGEN.</p>
        <p>Queen Alexandra is spending a pleasant holiday at her Danish home with her sister the Dowager Empress Marie of Russia. Her Majesty, according to present arrangements, will not be back in England till about the end of October. Our photo- graph shows t'le royal sisters on the steps of the Villa Hvidore, Copenhagen.</p>
        <p>TWENTY-FOUR HOURS'</p>
        <p>WALK.</p>
        <p>. Mr. T. Payne, of North Shields, won the Twenty-four hours' walking contest at the Stadium. All the best long-distance walkers entered, with the exception of F. E. Roberts, hut the champions dropped out early in the race- Mr. Payne covered 127 miles 542 Yards. .</p>
