      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-25_WidnesExaminer_art0130" n="art0130">
        <head>VI-COCOA FOR THE MOTHER.</head>
        <p>VI-COCOA FOR THE MOTHER.</p>
        <p>Vi-Cocoa will help Mother with her housework. It is just as good for her as it is for Father, and will save her just as much in food. Especially at lunch-time on washing day or when she begins to feel tired, a cup of Vi-Cocoa which takes very little time to make, will be found to help her more than you would believe.</p>
        <p>Nursing mothers should take</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-25_WidnesExaminer_art0131" n="art0131">
        <head>av--`E Cocoa'</head>
        <p>av--`E Cocoa'</p>
        <p>with plenty of milk in it. It is ever so much better for ,their purpose than stout, or oatmeal, or any of the things generally recommended.</p>
        <p>-.1917,,,Tenr tir-4 Wg</p>
        <p>You will not have sickly and ailing children—children that cry and wake you up at night—if you give them Vi- Cocoa—and a packet can be- / obtained from any grocer for sixpence—with their meal. This is proved. If you could see a child that has 'VI- C3COEI alongside of a child that doesn't, you would never have difficulty in saying which wa. which. The Vi-Cocoe boy or girl is always the rosier, healthier, fatter, more con- tented, more cheerful.</p>
      </div>
