        <p>• HOPPERS AT LUNCH. • The bop-picking season is now in full swing. There have been several blank days during the past fortnight, and so far as both hoppers and planters are concerned the suspension of operations adds to the effects of earlier misfortunes. Even in the best plantations the hops are less abundant than appearances indicated and not so finely developed. The hop-growing area is tecoming more nal more restricted. In the past two years the area has fallen from 44,938 to 32.539 acres, and the results of the present season are likely to lead to a further reduction. Our illustration shows one or two youthful hoppers buying cake for their mid-day meal. The gentleman with the basket is one of a party of Oxford undergraduates who are carrying on missionary work amongst the hoppers.</p>
