        <p>BOY LABOUR IN THE GENERAL POST-OFFICE. The Postmaster General has announced that with view to improving the prospects of the boy messengers employed by the post-office department to deliver telegrams, arrangements have been made to establish new classes of clerical assistants for employment in various towns. The scales of pay are not yet settled, but, beginning at Hs. a week, the "ago" pay and sub- sequent scale will probably be that of the sorting clerk and telegraphist class, as recommended last year by the Parliamentary Committee over which Mr. C. E. Hobhouse presided. The junior of these two classes is to be recruited frpm among the boy messengers between the ages of 10 and 19, and juniors who receive their appointment will be eligible for promotion to the senior class with age limits between 18 and 20.</p>
